{
  "name": "Colorectal Cancer (European Calibration)",
  "remarks": [
    "=======================================================================",
    "SYNTHEA MODULE: Colorectal Cancer — European Epidemiology Edition",
    "=======================================================================",
    "Calibrated against:",
    "  - ECIS / IARC GLOBOCAN 2020: Europe-specific incidence and survival",
    "  - ECDC Cancer Burden report 2022",
    "  - ESMO Clinical Practice Guidelines: Colorectal Cancer 2023",
    "  - EU Council Recommendation on cancer screening (2022)",
    "  - GBD 2019: Colon and rectum cancer — Europe",
    "  - Eurocare-6 survival study",
    "",
    "Key calibration data (ECIS/GLOBOCAN 2020 — Europe):",
    "  Colorectal cancer is the 2nd most common cancer in Europe by incidence",
    "  Age-standardised incidence: ~33 per 100,000 (both sexes)",
    "  Male ASR: ~42/100,000; Female ASR: ~26/100,000",
    "  5-year prevalence: ~0.7% of total population",
    "  Screening coverage (FIT/colonoscopy): highly variable by EU country",
    "  5-year survival (Eurocare-6): ~62% overall",
    "",
    "Age-specific incidence per 100,000/year (ECIS 2020):",
    "  45-49 years :  ~18",
    "  50-54 years :  ~38",
    "  55-59 years :  ~68",
    "  60-64 years : ~108",
    "  65-69 years : ~155",
    "  70-74 years : ~195",
    "  75-79 years : ~225",
    "R6 (2026-09-30): the module had NO Death state; End_CRC_Surveillance sent 5% per",
    "cycle to Terminal, which ends the module without killing anyone. Stage-specific",
    "excess mortality added from Eurocare-6, using the stage split already in the module.",
    "THE INCIDENCE IS DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED. It is ECIS age-specific incidence, listed",
    "band by band in the header above, and the generated data reproduce it (realised",
    "against coded: 0.98, 0.73, 0.96, 0.89, 0.91, 0.93, 1.01, 1.02). Changing mortality",
    "and incidence in one step would make the effect unattributable, and a life-table",
    "prediction of the pair is not trustworthy here: ECIS incidence combined with",
    "Eurocare survival under-produces ECIS prevalence by 24-31% in that model, so one of",
    "the three published quantities does not fit the other two. Measure first.",
    "Also corrected in the header's calibration notes: '5-year prevalence: ~0.7% of total",
    "population' is wrong. ECIS gives 0.635% COMPLETE prevalence for EU-27, and a",
    "five-year figure cannot exceed a complete one. The 0.7% in the verification table is",
    "within 10% of the complete prevalence, so that row survives - by coincidence, not by",
    "provenance. See R4-verification/sources/ecis-colorectal-2020.json.",
    "R6 pass two (2026-10-01): incidence adjusted, after the mortality from pass one was",
    "measured. Pass one alone moved 65-74 from +36% to -18% and 75+ from +29% to -34%",
    "against ECIS, so the survival was right in direction and the pair needed rebalancing.",
    "The published ECIS age gradient is kept INSIDE each coarse band and scaled by a",
    "factor fitted per band: x1.07 below 55, x0.88 at 55-64, x1.37 at 65-74, x1.72 at 75+.",
    "The 1.72 at 75+ has a clinical explanation rather than being a fudge: the header's",
    "incidence table stops at 75-79 with ~225 per 100,000 and R5 applied that flat to age",
    "100, while colorectal incidence keeps rising into the late eighties.",
    "Confidence differs by band. The model-to-data calibration factor was checked against",
    "two independent measurements - four pooled runs without mortality and the R6 run with",
    "it - and agrees to within 6% at 65-74 and 75+, the bands that carried the overshoot.",
    "It does NOT agree in the young bands (1.76 against 1.32 at 0-54), which hold 7 and 31",
    "cases, so the rates below 55 are the least certain part of this calibration.",
    "Expected after this change: 0-54 -40%, 55-64 -11%, 65-74 -4%, 75+ +1%. The residual",
    "at 0-54 is structural - ECIS counts from birth and this module starts at 40 - and is",
    "0.024 percentage points in absolute terms."
  ],
  "states": {
    "Initial": {
      "type": "Initial",
      "direct_transition": "Age_Guard"
    },
    "Age_Guard": {
      "type": "Guard",
      "allow": {
        "condition_type": "Age",
        "operator": ">=",
        "quantity": 40,
        "unit": "years"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Screening_Check",
      "remarks": [
        "Onset from 40, lowered from 45 in R6. Early-onset colorectal cancer is a real and",
        "rising share of the disease, and ECIS's 0-54 reference band contains cases a module",
        "starting at 45 cannot produce."
      ]
    },
    "Screening_Check": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "EU Council Recommendation 2022: FIT-based screening from age 50-74 across EU.",
        "Screening detection shifts stage distribution toward early-stage disease.",
        "~40% of European CRC detected through screening programmes."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.4,
          "transition": "CRC_Screening_Pathway"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.6,
          "transition": "CRC_Annual_Check"
        }
      ]
    },
    "CRC_Screening_Pathway": {
      "type": "Procedure",
      "remarks": [
        "FIT (faecal immunochemical test) — primary screening tool in most EU countries."
      ],
      "codes": [
        {
          "system": "SNOMED-CT",
          "code": "441579003",
          "display": "Measurement of occult blood in stool specimen using immunoassay (procedure)"
        }
      ],
      "duration": {
        "low": 5,
        "high": 10,
        "unit": "minutes"
      },
      "direct_transition": "CRC_Annual_Check"
    },
    "CRC_Annual_Check": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "conditional_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": "<",
            "quantity": 45,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Prob_40_44"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": "<",
            "quantity": 50,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Prob_45_49"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": "<",
            "quantity": 55,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Prob_50_54"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": "<",
            "quantity": 60,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Prob_55_59"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": "<",
            "quantity": 65,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Prob_60_64"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": "<",
            "quantity": 70,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Prob_65_69"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": "<",
            "quantity": 75,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Prob_70_74"
        },
        {
          "transition": "CRC_Prob_75_plus"
        }
      ]
    },
    "CRC_Annual_Delay": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "exact": {
        "quantity": 1,
        "unit": "years"
      },
      "direct_transition": "CRC_Annual_Check"
    },
