    "End_CRC_Surveillance": {
      "type": "EncounterEnd",
      "remarks": [
        "R5 sent 5% per cycle to Terminal. Terminal ends the MODULE; it does not kill the",
        "patient, so every colorectal cancer patient survived indefinitely and kept the",
        "diagnosis. This is the same defect found in lung_cancer_europe.json, and the",
        "module's own remarks cite the survival it never applied.",
        "Measured against ECIS EU-27 complete prevalence, index 2020, retrieved 2026-09-30:",
        "-31% at 0-54, +4% at 55-64, +36% at 65-74, +29% at 75+. The error grows with age,",
        "which is the signature of missing excess mortality, and the realised incidence",
        "matches the coded probability across every band (ratios 0.73-1.02), so it is not",
        "an incidence error."
      ],
      "direct_transition": "CRC_Outcome_Check"
    },
    "Terminal": {
      "type": "Terminal"
    },
    "CRC_Set_Stage_I": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "crc_stage",
      "value": "I",
      "direct_transition": "End_CRC_Encounter"
    },
    "CRC_Set_Stage_II": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "crc_stage",
      "value": "II",
      "direct_transition": "End_CRC_Encounter"
    },
    "CRC_Set_Stage_III": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "crc_stage",
      "value": "III",
      "direct_transition": "End_CRC_Encounter"
    },
    "CRC_Set_Stage_IV": {
      "type": "SetAttribute",
      "attribute": "crc_stage",
      "value": "IV",
      "direct_transition": "End_CRC_Encounter"
    },
    "CRC_Outcome_Check": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "Stage-specific excess mortality. Eurocare-6 five-year relative survival: stage I",
        "~90%, II ~80%, III ~70%, IV ~13%. Weighted by this module's own stage split",
        "(20/25/30/25) that is 62.3%, which is the ~62% the module header cites - the",
        "stage distribution and the survival figures were always mutually consistent, only",
        "unapplied.",
        "Relative survival already nets out background mortality, so it is exactly the",
        "excess term a prevalence model needs.",
        "Converted to a per-cycle probability at 2.667 follow-up cycles a year",
        "(CRC_Followup_Delay is 3-6 months): p = 1 - S5^(1/(5*cycles))."
      ],
      "conditional_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Attribute",
            "attribute": "crc_stage",
            "operator": "==",
            "value": "I"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Mortality_I"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Attribute",
            "attribute": "crc_stage",
            "operator": "==",
            "value": "II"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Mortality_II"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Attribute",
            "attribute": "crc_stage",
            "operator": "==",
            "value": "III"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Mortality_III"
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Attribute",
            "attribute": "crc_stage",
            "operator": "==",
            "value": "IV"
          },
          "transition": "CRC_Mortality_IV"
        },
        {
          "transition": "CRC_Mortality_III"
        }
      ]
    },
    "CRC_Mortality_I": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
